WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:11.440
"Low Protein Diets
for Parkinson's Disease"

00:00:11.440 --> 00:00:17.200
Parkinson's disease is a disease
of dopamine deficiency in the brain.

00:00:17.200 --> 00:00:20.400
You can't just have people take
dopamine because it can't

00:00:20.400 --> 00:00:22.240
pass through the blood-brain barrier,

00:00:22.240 --> 00:00:25.520
but you can give people
a dopamine precursor

00:00:25.520 --> 00:00:29.760
called levodopa, or L-dopa,
which can get up into the brain

00:00:29.760 --> 00:00:31.920
and be turned into dopamine.

00:00:31.920 --> 00:00:35.280
However, with prolonged treatment,
patients start to show a reduced

00:00:35.280 --> 00:00:39.600
response to levodopa. After
5 years of levodopa treatment,

00:00:39.600 --> 00:00:42.560
the benefits start wearing
off before the next dose,

00:00:42.560 --> 00:00:47.040
or don't completely contain symptoms
in a substantial proportion of patients,

00:00:47.040 --> 00:00:50.400
and represents a major source
of disability, and significantly

00:00:50.400 --> 00:00:55.520
impairs quality of life. Therefore,
maximizing the therapeutic efficiency

00:00:55.520 --> 00:00:59.360
of levodopa is an important
goal, and that's where

00:00:59.360 --> 00:01:03.520
protein-restricted diets come in.

00:01:03.520 --> 00:01:07.200
Wait, what does protein
have to do with Parkinson's?

00:01:07.200 --> 00:01:10.720
Certain amino acids in proteins
have been proven to impair

00:01:10.720 --> 00:01:14.400
the therapeutic effect of levodopa
by reducing its absorption

00:01:14.400 --> 00:01:17.040
and influx into the brain,
because they use

00:01:17.040 --> 00:01:20.000
the same transporter so
can crowd each other out.

00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:24.160
Here's a before-and-after PET
scan showing levodopa activity

00:01:24.160 --> 00:01:28.160
in the brain before and
after protein loading.

00:01:28.160 --> 00:01:32.960
That's why protein-restricted diets
can improve the efficacy of levodopa.

00:01:32.960 --> 00:01:37.200
There are three ways to do that:
an overall low-protein diet,

00:01:37.200 --> 00:01:42.720
a so-called protein-redistribution
diet, or a combination of the two.

00:01:42.720 --> 00:01:47.120
As a dietary strategy, 
a low-protein diet is nice because

00:01:47.120 --> 00:01:50.320
it's not only effective, but also
simple to understand and follow.

00:01:50.320 --> 00:01:56.400
And by low protein, we're just talking
about sticking to the recommended

00:01:56.400 --> 00:02:00.080
amount of protein, 0.8 grams
per kilogram of body weight.

00:02:00.080 --> 00:02:03.200
As I've covered before, most people
are eating excess protein

00:02:03.200 --> 00:02:05.200
and suffering because of it.

00:02:05.200 --> 00:02:10.960
0.8 grams per KG is equivalent
to about 0.36 grams per pound.

00:02:10.960 --> 00:02:15.600
So you take your weight in
pounds, multiply times 0.36,

00:02:15.600 --> 00:02:18.400
and get how many grams in
protein you should eat in a day.

00:02:18.400 --> 00:02:19.760
So if you weigh 140 pounds,

00:02:19.760 --> 00:02:22.640
you should eat about 50
grams of protein a day.

00:02:22.640 --> 00:02:26.080
The positive effect of limiting dietary
protein can be noticed within

00:02:26.080 --> 00:02:30.720
one week, even in patients no longer
responding to the manipulation

00:02:30.720 --> 00:02:35.520
of levodopa's medication schedule
or to other anti-Parkinson drugs.

00:02:35.520 --> 00:02:40.000
Protein-redistribution diets have
been investigated most thoroughly,

00:02:40.000 --> 00:02:41.120
and have been confirmed

00:02:41.120 --> 00:02:45.920
to be effective with a remarkable
60 to 100% response rate.

00:02:45.920 --> 00:02:48.640
We know about the deleterious
influence of dietary protein

00:02:48.640 --> 00:02:51.760
and the benefit of a low-protein
diet; however, it's not only

00:02:51.760 --> 00:02:55.600
the total amount of daily protein
but also how it's distributed

00:02:55.600 --> 00:03:00.000
over the day. If we eat only
protein-rich foods at night,

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:02.960
staying under a total of 10 grams
a day for breakfast and lunch,

00:03:02.960 --> 00:03:06.480
then we eliminate the amino
acid surges during the day,

00:03:06.480 --> 00:03:09.600
and who cares if they surge
after we go to bed?

00:03:09.600 --> 00:03:13.040
Parkinson's is a movement
disorder, and so if the drugs

00:03:13.040 --> 00:03:13.760
are not going to work,

00:03:13.760 --> 00:03:17.040
then it might as well be
when you're sleeping.

00:03:17.040 --> 00:03:20.400
Fiber is another way to
get levodopa to work better.

00:03:20.400 --> 00:03:22.720
Significant improvements
in L-dopa blood levels and

00:03:22.720 --> 00:03:26.320
Parkinson's symptoms starting
as early as 30 to 60 minutes

00:03:26.320 --> 00:03:28.160
after eating a diet rich

00:03:28.160 --> 00:03:33.200
in insoluble fiber, like the kind
found concentrated in whole grains.

00:03:33.200 --> 00:03:37.920
Well, if fiber helps, then how
about a plant-based diet

00:03:37.920 --> 00:03:40.880
for the management
of Parkinson's disease?

00:03:40.880 --> 00:03:45.600
You don't know until
you put it to the test.

00:03:45.600 --> 00:03:50.000
They looked at a normal protein
amount redistributed plant-based diet,

00:03:50.000 --> 00:03:52.880
and Parkinson's patients saw a
significant improvement in symptoms

00:03:52.880 --> 00:03:56.160
and performance, making it
a convenient way to conjugate

00:03:56.160 --> 00:03:59.120
the positive effects of
non-excess protein intake

00:03:59.120 --> 00:04:03.760
and a high fiber intake without
limiting total food amount.

00:04:03.760 --> 00:04:07.600
Planning such a diet is rather simple,
centering around unprocessed

00:04:07.600 --> 00:04:11.680
plant foods, but reserving protein-rich
plants like beans, split peas,

00:04:11.680 --> 00:04:14.720
chickpeas, lentils, and
peanuts to the evening meal.

00:04:14.720 --> 00:04:19.280
And voila --- the clinical improvement
hit all the major motor signs:

00:04:19.280 --> 00:04:22.320
the rigidity, the tremor, and
slowness of movement, 

00:04:22.320 --> 00:04:25.200
the things that really matter
to Parkinson's patients,

00:04:25.200 --> 00:04:29.520
in particular the tremor, the shaking,
which often does not respond

00:04:29.520 --> 00:04:33.920
to drugs but was highly positively
affected by the plant-based diet.

00:04:33.920 --> 00:04:37.200
So plants may be preferable
for Parkinson's,

00:04:37.200 --> 00:04:43.355
but you don't know how well it will
work for you until you give it a try.

